      "m",
      "This is the documentation for the Ruby-based AsciiDoc processor named Asciidoctor.\nAsciidoctor currently serves as the reference implementation for how to interpret the AsciiDoc language.\nIf you're looking for the documentation for the AsciiDoc language, see the xref:asciidoc::index.adoc[AsciiDoc section] of this website.",
