      "m",
      "Thanks to xref:asciidoctorj::index.adoc[AsciidoctorJ], Asciidoctor can be used in any program that runs on a Java Virtual Machine (JVM).\nUnder the covers, AsciidoctorJ uses JRuby to run Asciidoctor, but this is hidden behind a Java API.\nAsciidoctorJ even provides an alternate CLI, which means you can get the full Asciidoctor experience with only a Java runtime.\nBuilding atop AsciidoctorJ, there are also plugins that integrate Asciidoctor into Apache Maven, Gradle, or Javadoc builds.",
      Some([10, 53, -1, -1, 15, 39, 40, 52]),
