      "When we use the name \"`Asciidoctor`\" in this area of the documentation, we're referring to the core Asciidoctor Ruby processor, abbreviated as _Asciidoctor core_ or _Asciidoctor Ruby_.\nWe add the qualifier \"`core`\" because Asciidoctor is also the name of the suite of projects that provides runtimes, extensions, and tools for processing AsciiDoc.",
